        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Wait for channels to close before closing connections in disconnectPeers ex]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45610</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45610"/>
        <updated>2026-09-10T19:31:58.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #25424.">Fix</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="1629474651" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/25424" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/25424/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/25424">#25424</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">The key problem is that disconnection is asynchronous, but the current code treats it as synchronous, so there's a subtle race condition. Also as the issue describes, closing the connection makes the channel close happen abruptly without graceful shutdown.</p>
<p dir="auto">Made the function async to solve this problem.</p>]]></content>
