    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Move multi-paragraph descriptions out of the Try it section on HTML and WebAssembly pages]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45604</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45604"/>
        <updated>2026-09-10T17:20:10.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176228199?u=79263a5800d6a0c47f8ce53365fc113d033acaad&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">The last of four PRs splitting up <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5382179114" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45563" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/45563/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45563">#45563</a>. Draft, like <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5409965975" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45603" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/45603/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45603">#45603</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">These are the 28 HTML, WebAssembly and media pages where <strong>more than one paragraph</strong> sits after the <code class="notranslate">{{InteractiveExample}}</code> macro and therefore renders inside the "Try it" section. As currently written, each block moves up above the macro.</p>
<p dir="auto">The same open question as <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5409965975" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45603" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/45603/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45603">#45603</a> applies here — whether these belong above the demo or in a <code class="notranslate">## Description</code> section after it. Whatever is decided there, I will apply the same treatment to this PR, so it is probably easiest to settle it on <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5409965975" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45603" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/45603/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45603">#45603</a> alone.</p>
<p dir="auto">The largest cases are in this PR: <code class="notranslate">&lt;picture&gt;</code> and the <code class="notranslate">tabindex</code> global attribute both have eight paragraphs after the macro, which is well past the "very short summary" the template intends before the demo.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">Same underlying issue as <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5409960912" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45601" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/45601/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45601">#45601</a>: prose placed after the <code class="notranslate">{{InteractiveExample}}</code> macro renders inside the "Try it" section, after the demo's code, instead of reading as part of the page's description.</p>]]></content>
        <author>
            <name>husamemadH</name>
            <email>husamemadH@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/husamemadH</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2026-09-10T08:45:16.000Z</published>
    </entry>
    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Move multi-paragraph descriptions out of the Try it section on CSS pages]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45603</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45603"/>
        <updated>2026-09-10T15:53:01.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176228199?u=79263a5800d6a0c47f8ce53365fc113d033acaad&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">The third of four PRs splitting up <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5382179114" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45563" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/45563/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45563">#45563</a>. Draft until <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5409960912" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45601" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/45601/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45601">#45601</a> and <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5409963262" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45602" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/45602/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45602">#45602</a> are resolved, since this one raises a question those two don't.</p>
<p dir="auto">These are the 70 CSS pages where <strong>more than one paragraph</strong> sits after the <code class="notranslate">{{InteractiveExample}}</code> macro and therefore renders inside the "Try it" section. As currently written, this PR moves each block up above the macro, the same way as the single-sentence PRs.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>The open question:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45563#issuecomment-3389310786" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/45563/hovercard">in review on the previous PR</a> <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/wbamberg/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/wbamberg">@wbamberg</a> noted that the interactive example should come after a very short, preferably one-sentence summary, and that longer descriptions belong after the demo in a <code class="notranslate">## Description</code> section. <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/Josh-Cena/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/Josh-Cena">@Josh-Cena</a> agreed that discretion is needed, and that an intro which gets too long should be broken off into <code class="notranslate">## Description</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto">That applies to this PR rather than to <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5409960912" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45601" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/45601/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45601">#45601</a>/<a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5409963262" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45602" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/45602/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45602">#45602</a>. So before this is reviewed in detail, it would help to know which you'd prefer:</p>
<ol dir="auto">
<li>Move the paragraphs above the macro, as currently written.</li>
<li>Add a <code class="notranslate">## Description</code> section after the demo and put them there.</li>
<li>Decide per page, based on how long the intro becomes.</li>
</ol>
<p dir="auto">Only 4 of these 70 pages currently have a <code class="notranslate">## Description</code> section, so option 2 means adding the heading in most cases.</p>
<p dir="auto">For what it's worth, <code class="notranslate">list-style-type</code> was fixed upstream while this was in progress by adding a <code class="notranslate">## Description</code> section — so that appears to be the preferred shape. I have left that page and <code class="notranslate">list-style</code> out of this PR since they are already done.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">Same underlying issue as <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5409960912" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45601" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/45601/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45601">#45601</a>: prose placed after the <code class="notranslate">{{InteractiveExample}}</code> macro renders inside the "Try it" section, after the demo's code, instead of reading as part of the page's description.</p>]]></content>
