        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Correct createIndex exception wording]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45592</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45592"/>
        <updated>2026-09-09T14:29:42.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19912745?u=86e994bbf0f8db5235dd05517245916949ae48ac&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>

<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>

<p dir="auto"><a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/#dom-idbobjectstore-createindex" rel="nofollow">The spec</a> states:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">If an <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/#index-concept" rel="nofollow">index</a> <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/#index-name" rel="nofollow">named</a> name already exists in store, <a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-throw" rel="nofollow">throw</a> a "<a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#constrainterror" rel="nofollow">ConstraintError</a>" <a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-DOMException" rel="nofollow">DOMException</a>.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">I have changed the docs to refer to the object store rather than the database.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

<p dir="auto">This confused me when reading as a newbie to IndexedDB</p>]]></content>
